# canonicalize (Function)

Validates and normalizes service metadata into a consistent typed structure.

Pass a context object with identity, ownership, and optional environment and governance fields. The function checks all string values for correctness, rejects invalid input, and returns the same structure in canonical form. If governance is empty, it is omitted from the output.

## Example Usage

### Basic

```terraform
output "context" {
  value = provider::platctx::canonicalize({
    identity = {
      name      = "payments"
      namespace = "platform"
    }
    ownership = {
      owned_by    = "team:platform"
      operated_by = "team:sre"
    }
  })
}
```

### With Governance

```terraform
output "context" {
  value = provider::platctx::canonicalize({
    identity = {
      name      = "payments"
      namespace = "platform"
    }
    ownership = {
      owned_by    = "team:platform"
      operated_by = "team:sre"
    }
    environment = "production"
    governance = {
      criticality         = "critical"
      cost_center         = "CC-FIN-001"
      data_classification = "internal"
    }
  })
}
```

### Consumed by a Module

Use the canonicalized output to feed service metadata into a platform module:

```terraform
locals {
  ctx = provider::platctx::canonicalize({
    identity = {
      name      = "payments"
      namespace = "platform"
    }
    ownership = {
      owned_by    = "team:platform"
      operated_by = "team:sre"
    }
    environment = "production"
    governance = {
      criticality         = "critical"
      cost_center         = "CC-FIN-001"
      data_classification = "internal"
    }
  })
}

module "service" {
  source = "./modules/platform/service"

  name                = local.ctx.identity.name
  namespace           = local.ctx.identity.namespace
  owner               = local.ctx.ownership.owned_by
  operator            = local.ctx.ownership.operated_by
  environment         = local.ctx.environment
  criticality         = local.ctx.governance.criticality
  cost_center         = local.ctx.governance.cost_center
  data_classification = local.ctx.governance.data_classification
}
```

This pattern works across cloud providers and modules. The same context object passes cleanly downstream regardless of which resources the module creates.

